  "query_preview": "stretch of dry and seasonable weather this week.\nTonight won't be as cold as the past few nights have been, but\nwe should still see temperatures drop into the upper 30s and low\n40s. Patchy frost will be possible in the coldest spots, but not\nin the areas where the growing season is still active. The \nlatest model data shows the dry spell continuing into the final \nweek of October. This rain-free pattern will feature a string \nof sunny and seasonably warm afternoons with low humidity \nfollowed by clear and chilly moonlit nights with areas of frost.",
